{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":279031,"duration_api_ms":421365,"num_turns":18,"result":"All checks pass. The implementation is complete. Let me produce the execution payload.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Split periphyton and decomposer biomass from single lumped pools into per-habitat BTreeMap<HabitatKind, f64> pools across all 5 habitats (FilterMedia, GlassHardscape, PlantSurfaces, SubstrateSurface, SubstrateDeep). Periphyton growth in algae_growth.rs now iterates per-habitat with independent light factors, capacity, and loss calculations. Decomposer kinetics in nitrogen_cycle.rs distribute growth/decay proportionally using per-habitat oxygen exposure weighting. Grazing (shrimp, microfauna) draws from all habitat pools proportionally via shared remove_periphyton_proportionally(). Save schema bumped to v11 with serde(default) migration. Invariants validate all per-habitat values are non-negative. 10 dedicated tests cover split correctness, conservation, growth divergence, grazing targeting, save/load roundtrip, and habitat diversity effects.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"description\": \"Add per-habitat biomass pools to AlgaeState (periphyton_by_habitat: BTreeMap<HabitatKind, f64>) and MicrobeState (decomposer_by_habitat: BTreeMap<HabitatKind, f64>) in biology.rs, with sync/set/distribute methods and ecologically-weighted affinity functions (light-driven for periphyton, flow+oxygen-driven for decomposers)\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"description\": \"Add ensure_habitat_pools() to TankState (state.rs) called from refresh_habitat_registry(), distributing lumped totals into per-habitat maps when maps are empty (migration/first-run path)\",\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"description\": \"Rewrite periphyton growth in algae_growth.rs from single aggregate calculation to per-habitat loop: each habitat in